uires clicking the third result and we cannot proceed otherwise.\n\n4) The click on the article's link/heading is expected to navigate away, so I make that the final action in the function.\n\nRegarding other knowledge-base functions: create_curated_collection_and_newsletter is not appropriate for this task because it wraps the search helper and additional newsletter creation; it's not necessary for simply performing a search and clicking the third result, so I did not use it.\n\nThis approach follows the accessibility-tree-centric selectors and uses the required knowledge-base helper.\n</reasoning>\n\n<code>\nasync def act(page):\n    \"\"\"\n    Plan:\n    1. Use the site-aware helper create_curated_collection_by_search to drive the visible\n       search widget and search for the keyword 'reveals'. This helper is required by\n       the instructions when a matching knowledge-base function exists and it handles\n       locating the complementary search UI, activating the search, and waiting for\n       results to render.\n    2. After the helper returns (results are rendered in role=\"main\" as role=\"article\" children),\n       locate the third article (index 2) and click the first link inside that article.\n       If there is no link, fall back to clicking a heading inside the article if present.\n\n    Notes:\n    - The helper will call await page.goto('/') as its first action; this is acceptable\n      from the current state and ensures a reproducible starting point for the search.\n    - Clicking the result is expected to navigate away, so the click is the last action.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 1) Use the site-aware helper to perform the visible search for 'reveals'\n    await create_curated_collection_by_search(page, \"reveals\")\n\n    # 2) Locate articles inside the main region and ensure there are at least 3\n    main = page.get_by_role(\"main\")\n    articles = main.get_by_role(\"article\")\n    count = await articles.count()\n    if count < 3:\n        raise 